  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to deduct; to subtract",
      "explanation": "To remove an amount from a total, typically in financial or mathematical contexts."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to balance; to offset",
      "explanation": "To consider both positive and negative factors and arrive at a net result."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06701_sashihiku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{税金|ぜいきん}を{差|さ}し{引|ひ}く。",
      "english": "To deduct taxes.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06701_sashihiku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{経費|けいひ}を{差|さ}し{引|ひ}くと{利益|りえき}はほとんどない。",
      "english": "After deducting expenses, there's almost no profit.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06701_sashihiku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{税金|ぜいきん}を{差|さ}し{引|ひ}いた{手取|てど}りは{20万円|にじゅうまんえん}です。",
      "english": "The take-home pay after deducting taxes is 200,000 yen.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06701_sashihiku_ex4",
      "japanese": "{差|さ}し{引|ひ}きゼロだ。",
      "english": "It balances out to zero.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06701_sashihiku_ex5",
      "japanese": "{良|よ}いところも{悪|わる}いところも{差|さ}し{引|ひ}いて{考|かんが}えると、{悪|わる}くない{条件|じょうけん}だ。",
      "english": "Balancing the good and the bad, it's not a bad deal.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06701_sashihiku_ex6",
      "japanese": "{苦労|くろう}も{多|おお}かったが、{差|さ}し{引|ひ}きすれば{楽|たの}しい{経験|けいけん}だった。",
      "english": "There were many hardships, but on balance it was an enjoyable experience.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "CONJUGATION:\n・{差|さ}し{引|ひ}く → {差|さ}し{引|ひ}かない (negative)\n・{差|さ}し{引|ひ}く → {差|さ}し{引|ひ}いて (te-form)\n・{差|さ}し{引|ひ}く → {差|さ}し{引|ひ}いた (past)\n\nFORMATION:\nCompound verb: {差|さ}す (to insert) + {引|ひ}く (to pull/subtract)\n\nRELATED EXPRESSIONS:\n・{差|さ}し{引|ひ}き - noun form meaning \"deduction\" or \"balance\"\n・{差|さ}し{引|ひ}き{勘定|かんじょう} - net calculation/balance\n・{差|さ}し{引|ひ}きゼロ - balances out to zero\n\nUSAGE:\nCommonly used in financial and business contexts:\n・{源泉徴収|げんせんちょうしゅう}を{差|さ}し{引|ひ}く (to deduct withholding tax)\n・{割引|わりびき}を{差|さ}し{引|ひ}く (to deduct a discount)",
